  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Calcium gluconate may interact with U373 MG through a series of molecular targets, primarily Toll-like receptor 6. This receptor is targeted by multiple compounds, including 6-[(11-carboxy-4,4,6a,6b,8a,11,14b-heptamethyl-14-oxo-2,3,4a,5,6,7,8,9,10,12,12a,14a-dodecahydro-1H-picen-3-yl)oxy]-3,4-dihydroxy-5-(3,4,5-trihydroxyoxan-2-yl)oxyoxane-2-carboxylic acid and 3-(4-Chlorophenoxy)-2-hydroxypropanoic acid. These compounds are all capable of targeting Toll-like receptor 6, which in turn is a target of Saquayamycin G, another compound that also leads to U373 MG. The scores for these relationships are consistent, indicating a potential role for Calcium gluconate in modulating the activity of these targets, which may ultimately influence the behavior of U373 MG cells. The evidence suggests a possible mechanism by which Calcium gluconate could interact with U373 MG, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
